# CFD From Scratch: 1D Advection Solvers

A collection of 1D finite difference solvers developed from first principles in Python.

The objective of this repository is to build a complete understanding of numerical methods used in CFD, beginning with the linear advection equation and progressing toward diffusion, advection-diffusion, implicit methods, matrix-based solvers, and eventually Navier-Stokes equations.

---

# Governing Equation

The 1D Linear Advection Equation:

\[
\frac{\partial u}{\partial t}
+
c\frac{\partial u}{\partial x}
=
0
\]

where:

- \(u\) = transported variable
- \(c\) = advection velocity

---

# Numerical Method

## Time Discretization

Forward Difference

\[
\frac{\partial u}{\partial t}
\approx
\frac{u_i^{n+1}-u_i^n}{\Delta t}
\]

## Space Discretization

Central Difference

\[
\frac{\partial u}{\partial x}
\approx
\frac{u_{i+1}^{n}-u_{i-1}^{n}}
{2\Delta x}
\]

Substituting into the PDE gives:

\[
u_i^{n+1}
=
u_i^n
-\frac{Co}{2}
\left(
u_{i+1}^{n}
-
u_{i-1}^{n}
\right)
\]

where:

\[
Co=\frac{c\Delta t}{\Delta x}
\]

is the Courant Number.

